---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";

const toc = [
  { label: "The team workspace", href: "#workspace" },
  { label: "Task lifecycle", href: "#lifecycle" },
  { label: "Reviews and approvals", href: "#reviews" },
  { label: "Ownership and history", href: "#ownership" },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Teams"
  description="Coordinate people and coding agents around tasks, runs, diffs, checkpoints, reviews, approvals, and merges."
  currentPath="/docs/teams"
  eyebrow="Product"
  {toc}
>
  <section id="workspace">
    <h2>The team workspace</h2>
    <p>
      Modesto Teams is a work surface, not a chat room. Each project is
      organized around executable tasks and their evidence: agent runs,
      changed files, checks, checkpoints, review findings, decisions, and merge
      state.
    </p>
    <div class="docs-callout"><strong>Conversation stays attached to work.</strong><p>Comments and decisions live beside the task, diff, or checkpoint they concern, so the team does not have to reconstruct intent from a separate message stream.</p></div>
  </section>

  <section id="lifecycle">
    <h2>A task from assignment to merge</h2>
    <div class="docs-steps">
      <article><div><h3>Define the outcome</h3><p>Create a task with scope, acceptance criteria, repository context, and an owner.</p></div></article>
      <article><div><h3>Run an agent</h3><p>Start work with an approved provider, model, permission policy, and checkout strategy.</p></div></article>
      <article><div><h3>Checkpoint progress</h3><p>Capture the diff, validation state, incomplete work, and next step before changing ownership or provider.</p></div></article>
      <article><div><h3>Review the evidence</h3><p>Inspect the implementation, checks, agent findings, and human feedback in the same task.</p></div></article>
      <article><div><h3>Approve and merge</h3><p>Record the decision and merge only when repository policy and required approvals allow it.</p></div></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="reviews">
    <h2>Reviews and approvals</h2>
    <div class="docs-table">
      <div><strong>Needs review</strong><span>The run produced changes or findings that require a person to inspect.</span></div>
      <div><strong>Changes requested</strong><span>Feedback is attached to the relevant diff or task and the work returns to an agent or owner.</span></div>
      <div><strong>Approved</strong><span>The recorded reviewer accepted the current revision; later material changes can require another review.</span></div>
      <div><strong>Merged</strong><span>The accepted work reached the target branch under the repository’s merge policy.</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="ownership">
    <h2>Ownership and complete history</h2>
    <p>
      Every handoff should identify who or what owns the next action. The task
      timeline keeps provider runs, checkpoints, review decisions, and merges
      ordered so a teammate can understand both the current state and how it
      was reached.
    </p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
